# Shell scripts and the docker config they source MUST be LF, whatever the checkout platform does.
# A CRLF entrypoint.sh makes the container fail at exec with the famously unhelpful
# "exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory" — the kernel is reporting that
# "/bin/bash\r" does not exist, not the script. Observed 2026-08-10 on a Windows checkout.
*.sh            text eol=lf
docker/**       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
